WEBVTT

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:03.400
My passionate Idol Activities,

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.340
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:13.200
We eight members of STAR☆ANIS worked hard to make our hearts as one.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.570
We traveled to stadiums all over the country,

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.650
met a whole bunch of fans,

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.200
and received power from each of them.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.710
But no matter how much of that power we used,

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:27.710
no matter how hot and bright we all burned, {some will dispute it, but I feel strongly that "burn" can be a linking verb}

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:30.710
it grew and grew until it filled each and every stadium we visited. {to make it long enough to avoid the logo}

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:34.970
And now, at the end of our summer tour,

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:42.850
all eight of us are completely burnt out.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:47.480
Girls, I'm so proud of you all.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.860
Today, the concert, the fans,

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.150
even the weather and everything else...

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:53.490
...were like a miracle!

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.860
Yeah!

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.660
I never wanted to leave the stage.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.660
I know, I felt like I wanted to be up there forever.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.620
I guess that's about it for our summer tour.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:11.670
Way to drain all their blood in one fell swoop, Ran.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.590
Geez, Ran!

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:14.630
S-Sorry.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:20.720
There is one last thing I have yet to tell you.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.560
Although your summer tour may have officially ended,

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:26.230
I've set up one last secret live concert for you.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.860
Our tour's not over yet!

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:33.940
<i>Looks like we're not burned out yet!</i>

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.630
The tickets for the secret live

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:15.900
were given out via raffle to fifty pairs of two people each

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.880
at concert halls and CD shops.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:19.760
One hundred fans?

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.590
It's hard to place how many that is after all our concerts.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.640
That sounds like a big downgrade in scale.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:30.390
On the other hand, we'll be able to get closer to our fans than ever before.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:33.020
We're on our way to the stage right now.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.710
I'll leave everything about this performance up to you girls.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.400
It's pitch black outside.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:46.530
But isn't it still early in the afternoon?

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:52.040
What happened?

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.830
Where are we?

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:11.530
STAR☆ANIS, thank you for your stadium tour!

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:12.260
Fans! {life goal, never translate "minna" in the vocative as "everyone"}

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:13.230
Incredible.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.440
Surprise! {oh Kaede}

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:22.160
I didn't see this one coming!

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:27.180
Yurika-sama, your glasses!

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:30.790
S-Surprise me again and I'll suck your blood.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:36.300
Each one of you has been blessed by the goddess of luck and won a ticket.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:39.810
You will now join STAR☆ANIS on this cruise ship

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:42.340
as we sail for Tokyo.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:50.400
Tomorrow evening, we will hold a concert on the main deck. {or evening, but not night}

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:56.350
Until then, please enjoy all the fun events we've prepared for you throughout the day.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:59.360
Prepare yourselves, STAR☆ANIS!

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.510
This secret live wasn't just a surprise for us,

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:09.360
but also an event that will become an unforgettable memory.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:14.290
We're looking forward to spending time with the fans who have supported us all this time.

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:20.180
Whenever we go on stage as STAR☆ANIS, there's a particular phrase we like say together...

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:21.110
I know!

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:22.910
I saw it on TV!

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:25.010
Then join us as we say...

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:26.550
STAR☆ANIS...

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.990
Start! {not much of an aikotoba}

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:36.810
I'd like to use the same songs in the same order as we have been at our stadium concerts,

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:39.320
but there's not quite enough time.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:45.020
That's why I propose combining our songs in the middle into a medley so that we can get through them all.

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:46.110
What do you think?

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.600
Sounds good.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:51.780
Mizuki-san, no matter what challenges you're faced with, you never panic.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:52.580
You're great!

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:55.830
How could I? We've got a concert tomorrow.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:06:00.860
As the leader of Powa Powa Puririn, Otome looks up to you, Mizuki-san.

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:04.380
Mizuki-sama is our guardian angel.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:06.510
Flattery will get you nowhere, you know.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:14.970
That's your schedule for tomorrow.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:16.890
But these events...

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:23.780
Are you okay, Ichigo?

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:27.620
You've been nodding this whole time, but do you really get it?

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.900
I get that it'll be really fun!

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:31.450
You know how to get to the point.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:33.870
But still...

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:35.370
It's a hard schedule!

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:40.880
This means that our secret live has already begun, doesn't it, Headmistress Orihime?

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:43.960
I knew you'd understand.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:47.780
This secret live is more than just a concert—

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:50.530
it encompasses this entire cruise.

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:52.260
Correct?

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.790
I'm not forcing you do anything,

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:59.310
but I've made sure to prepare plenty of 
opportunities to interact with your fans.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:01.270
The rest is up to you.

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:03.020
So that's why you said,

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:06.030
Prepare yourselves, STAR☆ANIS!

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:07.780
isn't it?

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:10.280
It's different from when we perform in a huge stadium.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:14.860
Right now, our fans are standing within our reach.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:16.290
In other words...

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:19.280
It's as if they're standing alongside us on stage.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:25.530
An idol who keeps a large discrepancy
 between her activities and her true self

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:28.150
will one day be swallowed into that abyss.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:32.590
That's why I want you all to show your fans who you really are from the start.

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:37.250
It may even become a chance for you to spread your wings even further.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.610
Thank you, Headmistress.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:46.770
Starting now, STAR☆ANIS will shift from unit activities to individual activities.

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:50.530
<i>We'll be doing things by ourselves instead of together?</i>

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:54.720
As the headmistress said, when we're not on stage,

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:57.680
we should act like our usual selves.

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:00.040
That's it for today's meeting.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:09.340
Mizuki-san, why the sudden change?

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:18.450
I'm about to have a meeting with our staff in Shanghai about Tristar's next promotion.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:24.020
So our time as teammates comes to an end.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:27.200
If you have time, I'd like you to participate.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:28.770
Not a problem.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:33.280
I feel like Mizuki-san just set off on another one of her long journeys.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:37.440
I'm sure she has a good reason for doing all this.

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:40.770
That's right. All good things come to an end.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:44.290
Not just this tour, but all of our activities as a unit.

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:48.500
I feel like she's telling us to do everything we can today for an even brighter tomorrow.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:49.680
That's so cool!

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.290
Yeah, it sure is.

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:54.740
Are both of you fine with this?

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:57.570
We're not "fine", but there's nothing we can do.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:59.970
We can't forget about Soleil either.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:01.520
So stop sulking, Ichigo!

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:02.770
Ow-ow-ow... {This is surprising the optimal punctuation}

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:06.170
I'm gonna head back to my own room now.

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:08.050
Gotta get ready for tomorrow. {練る, not 寝る}

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:10.780
I'm about to head to the restaurant, so come with me for a bit.

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:13.990
What's wrong, Aoi? You hungry already?

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:15.350
Wrong!

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:18.200
I just thought up a great fan service idea! {can technically mean other stuff too} {not just technically, either}

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.180
Stop stalling, just tell me already.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:31.590
I wish I could continue this tour with Mizuki-san and everyone else forever.

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:36.960
Sakura-tan, our tour is finally going to end tomorrow.

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:39.720
Yes, I feel like it passed in the blink of an eye.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:45.350
Our experience with STAR☆ANIS will be useful when we return to Powa Powa Puririn. {who are you, Otome?} {she might have said something smart, but she's still Otome and can't use long sentences}

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:48.770
Yes. All the lessons I learned from my senpai

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:52.440
will allow me to perform even better in Powa Powa Puririn.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:58.010
Sakura-tan, our glorious return to Powa Powa Puririn is going to be so much fun!

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:00.720
I couldn't agree more.

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:12.460
Did you really believe you could sneak up on Yurika-sama?

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:14.880
I am the immortal vampire...

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:17.380
Toudou Yurika!

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:21.260
Aoi, are those coasters?

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:24.390
I think it'd be nice to give these out tomorrow.

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:28.680
Like Mizuki-san said, the way to a successful secret live

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:33.150
lies in us personally interacting with each of our fans.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:34.810
You just blew my mind...

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:38.330
Aoi, you're like a professional producer.

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:40.560
You should be doing something, too.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:41.410
Yeah...

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:50.560
Who's there?

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:51.710
It's Ichigo.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:54.000
Strawberry! Coming!

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:56.170
What happened?

00:10:56.850 --> 00:11:01.640
Well, I just remembered that I still had this handkerchief you lent me...

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:04.200
Why, thank you.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:09.390
Sorry, looks like I stopped you from going to bed.

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:12.440
No problem, just hang on a sec.

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:18.780
Sorry, Yurika had just gone to bed, so I couldn't invite you in.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:21.080
Now then, I'll be entering my eternal rest.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:22.660
Oh, good night.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.840
No, that's my fault.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.790
The truth is that I wanted to talk with you.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:28.860
With me?

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:29.660
Yep.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:33.710
You surprised me over and over throughout this entire tour.

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:36.960
Really? Which performances surprised you?

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:45.450
So the reason you came over was to get back at me for those times.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:46.850
That might be true.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:51.950
"STAR☆ANIS will shift from unit activities to individual activities."

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:55.650
I can't get Mizuki-san's words out of my head.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:12:01.010
Everyone's already accepted her words and started looking forward to the future, but I'm still...

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:02.680
Are you feeling lonely?

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:04.740
Maybe.

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:06.280
Okay!

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:08.760
I grew up in the USA!

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:11.790
So if you please, I will now tell you the story of my American Aikatsu.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:13.040
Sure!

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:17.300
In America, there is a single road to passing auditions.

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:22.170
Even the big stars and super idols all start the same way.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:25.300
Everyone starts out doing all sorts of part-time jobs,

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:30.560
all the while sticking close to a good coach and taking lessons day and night.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.310
I never knew.

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:38.310
We travel to the ends of the country, carrying little more than our profile pics and our Aikatsu cards.

00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:40.570
That's the same as us!

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:44.360
However, there are hundreds, thousands of people

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:49.680
all competing against each other for a single position in this ruthless world!

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:52.080
And if you catch the waves of luck,

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:55.020
you may be able to keep it up for ten years!

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:57.310
You'll be a movie star millionaire!

00:12:57.310 --> 00:13:02.080
There awaits you a summer home in the southern isles, and a private jet to do your shopping with!

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.220
Becoming a celeb wouldn't just be a dream!

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:08.910
But if your popularity starts to drop,

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:11.470
you'll be back on the streets in a flash.

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:13.170
I can't even imagine a world like that.

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:16.230
Most strangers look at me and see my rich father

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:18.980
and think I've been raised without a single worry in the world.

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:22.980
I've been a regular on idol programs since I was a child,

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:27.340
and those people think I'm a girl who's never worked a day in her life. {correct who form?} {yes}

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:31.490
But if that were true, I never would've become a real idol.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:32.750
Yeah.

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:36.930
It's only because I was surrounded by people who were always trying their best

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:40.200
that I understood how much harder than them I'd have to work.

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:43.850
All of my rich friends thought that I was crazy.

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:47.510
They said that I'd be able to live a happy life just by sitting on my butt.

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:52.960
But it was because I believed in the abilities I had

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:57.100
that I was able to stand on stage and entertain so many people.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:01.270
I believed that I had the power to make people happy within me.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:06.690
Whether you're alone or with your friends, believe in yourself.

00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:10.100
Believe in the same way that you trust your friends.

00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:11.990
Believe in myself...

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:14.840
That way, you'll never be lonely or scared.

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:23.150
<i>Kaede-chan came to Japan all by herself, yet she's still shining so brightly.</i>

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:24.850
<i>"Believe in yourself"...</i>

00:14:25.390 --> 00:14:28.640
<i>Mizuki-san and the others already do.</i>

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:30.370
<i>And so I, too...</i>

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:32.720
<i>will believe in myself.</i>

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:50.450
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:56.950
I curse the morning sun.

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:58.070
Mizuki-san!

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:58.930
Ran-chan!

00:14:58.070 --> 00:14:59.710
You can do it!

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:03.960
Aikatsu, Aikatsu...

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:07.960
Kaede-chan's incredible!

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:09.520
I'll do it too!

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:10.930
Ai— ah!

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:13.400
My back!

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:15.260
It's because you don't stretch enough.

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:18.230
You need to <i>bend</i> your body, not break it.

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:27.750
They're signed!

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:28.990
Awesome!

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:32.980
Ichigo-chan, what kind of books do you like?

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:36.490
Let's see... I read a lot of cookbooks.

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:39.830
Oh, but I like actually cooking more than reading about it.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:44.000
No, forget about cooking, I like eating the most!

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.300
We've been to every single one of your stadium concerts!

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:49.070
We traveled all across the country!

00:15:49.070 --> 00:15:50.330
What, seriously?

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:52.230
When did they have that power outage?

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:55.510
Opening day. We couldn't believe our eyes!

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:57.250
I won't ever forget that.

00:15:57.250 --> 00:16:00.520
We're sorry for worrying you so much that day.

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:04.810
Ichigo-chan.

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:07.120
What's your name?

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:08.320
Are you by yourself?

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:11.110
Rion. I came with Onii-chan.

00:16:13.060 --> 00:16:14.320
That's great!

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:18.060
Rion wants to be an idol just like you!

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:19.410
Wow, really?

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:25.420
Thanks!

00:16:27.490 --> 00:16:28.670
<i>Mizuki-san...</i>

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:30.320
I must be off now. {or I have to go}

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:32.450
Let's talk again later.

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:37.390
Mizuki-chan...

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:41.360
It's like Mizuki-san's table is in a world of its own.

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:43.640
Powa Powa...

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:45.150
Puririn!

00:16:50.590 --> 00:16:55.160
Otome-chan, Sakura-chan, and even Yurika-chan are incredible in their own way.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.720
Ichigo, you done eating yet?

00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:58.960
We've gotta go.

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:01.580
Wait, I haven't even eaten a piece of bread yet.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:04.610
It's time for the dance lesson, so save it until after.

00:17:04.610 --> 00:17:06.430
Good, now stand up.

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:10.300
My bread!

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:11.820
Ichigo-chan, here!

00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:13.550
Thank you!

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:14.590
Go for it!

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:15.170
Hang in there!

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:16.050
Fight!

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:23.680
The focus of today's lesson will be the choreography for our new medley.

00:17:24.010 --> 00:17:27.230
By the way, who's going to be leading the lesson?

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:30.150
I haven't seen you-know-who at all yet.

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:33.220
What's that sound?

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:35.700
P-Pirates?!

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:39.450
Hey hey hey, STAR☆ANIS-honeys! {holy shit}

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:43.580
I can't believe you'd leave 
Captain Johnny behind like this.

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:47.580
Ho ho ho!

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:56.690
Hey, anyone who wants to learn how to dance,

00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:58.090
don't be shy—come on.

00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:01.690
Ichigo-chan.

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:04.370
Rion-chan! Want to dance together?

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:05.360
Sure!

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:07.730
We want to make some good summer memories too!

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:08.670
Great!

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:10.610
We're in your care, Captain.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:13.110
All right, let's dance!

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:27.460
All that's left is the concert itself.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:31.310
Does anybody have any regrets?

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:32.280
I do!

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:34.590
Hoshimiya?

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:40.140
I think I finally understood why you told us to do things individually.

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:41.850
You have?

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:46.030
That let our fans come to and interact with each one of us by ourselves,

00:18:46.030 --> 00:18:51.880
which made them feel even closer to STAR☆ANIS, and in turn come to love us more.

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:53.860
I hope we made that happen.

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:58.860
Yeah! At least, that's how I've fallen more in love with STAR☆ANIS.

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:03.700
We've been on this tour together all summer, but once I took a step back and looked again,

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:09.460
I realized just how amazing all of us are!

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:11.150
Hoshimiya...

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:16.510
That's why I'm really grateful that you had us go out on our own.

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:17.930
That means a lot.

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:21.110
Our summer tour is almost at its close.

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:24.220
STAR☆ANIS will break up back into Tristar,

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.850
Powa Powa Puririn,

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:27.850
and Soleil.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:31.820
I wanted to take the power that we all brought together for this tour

00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:35.790
and return it to each of our individual hands

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:40.360
in order not to forget that each of us was in STAR☆ANIS as individuals.

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:44.120
Until we leave this boat, we are STAR☆ANIS!

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:50.150
Let's finish this up with more energy than all of our past concerts combined!

00:19:50.150 --> 00:19:51.620
Okay, Mizuki-san!

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:53.130
STAR☆ANIS...

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:54.880
Start!

00:22:12.820 --> 00:22:13.720
See you.

00:22:13.720 --> 00:22:14.850
Bye!

00:23:55.650 --> 00:23:57.740
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:01.380
Yurika, you can't sleep anywhere outside your coffin?

00:24:01.380 --> 00:24:02.640
Of course.

00:24:02.640 --> 00:24:05.570
A good sleep is the first step to good health.

00:24:05.570 --> 00:24:07.420
Yes, you got it!

00:24:07.900 --> 00:24:09.880
Good sleep begins with a bed!

00:24:10.680 --> 00:24:13.230
Shion-sama seems to be depressed.

00:24:13.230 --> 00:24:16.140
She must be worrying about something important!

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:18.550
Seven faces aren't enough anymore.

00:24:18.550 --> 00:24:19.810
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:19.810 --> 00:24:21.480
Idol in Wonderland!

00:24:21.480 --> 00:24:25.460
Always passionate, Idol Activities!
